layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Photo Albums
permalink: /albums/
---

						<div align="center">
							<table border="0" cellspacing="5" cellpadding="5" width="600">
								<tr>
									<td style="border:solid 2px #000000;" colspan="2" align="left" valign="middle" bgcolor="#ffffff">
										<p class="photoTitle" style="text-align:center;margin-left:30;margin-right:30;">Chloe, Owen, and Macy's Photo Albums</p>
										<p class="default" style="margin-left:30;margin-right:30;">Okay. So, I've finally organized all of the photos into albums. The most recent photo albums are at the top of the page, and each album contains anywhere from 7 to 40 photos. If you don't like the "album" organization, you can click <a class="defaultLink" href="/photos/">here</a> to see all of the photos (currently <span style="color:#8C3312;">{{ gallery.photos.length }}</span> of them) on a single page. But there are so many photos that this can be kind of cumbersome.</p>
									</td>
								</tr>
{%- for album in gallery.albums | reverse %}
								<tr></tr>
								<tr>
									<td style="border:solid 2px #000000;" width="220" height="220" align="center" valign="middle" bgcolor="#ffffff"><a href="/albums/{{ album.number }}/"><img src="/images/albums/{{ album.cover }}.jpg" border="0"></a></td>
									<td style="border:solid 2px #000000;" height="220" align="left" valign="middle" bgcolor="#ffffff"><p class="photoTitle" style="margin-left:30;">Album #{{ album.number }}</p><p class="default" style="margin-left:30;">{{ album.descriptionHtml | safe }}</p><a class="defaultLink" style="margin-left:30;" href="/albums/{{ album.number }}/">View Album</a></td>
								</tr>
{%- endfor %}
								<tr></tr>
							</table>
						</div>
						<br><br>
